# Superpowers

This repo uses [obra/superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers) v6.3.0 as the agent development methodology. Skills live in `.cursor/skills/`.

Hospital platform rules (`.cursor/rules/00`–`12`, IP/Billing/Ward SoT, Figma MCP) take precedence over Superpowers when they conflict. Superpowers is process; those rules are domain, safety, and architecture.

## Invoke skills before acting

If there is even a small chance a skill applies, read that skill's `SKILL.md` and follow it before responding, exploring, or writing code. Announce `Using [skill] to [purpose]`.

| Request | Skill |
|---|---|
| New feature, screen, behavior, or "let's build X" | `brainstorming` first (hard gate: no implementation until approved) |
| Bug / unexpected behavior | `systematic-debugging` |
| Approved design / multi-step work | `writing-plans` then `subagent-driven-development` or `executing-plans` |
| Implementation | `test-driven-development` using existing Vitest / Playwright `e2e/` / .NET tests (`12-testing-validation.mdc`) |
| "Is it actually done?" | `verification-before-completion` |
| Review / finish a branch | `requesting-code-review` / `finishing-a-development-branch` |

Do not skip brainstorming by calling a change "too simple." Bounded work still needs a short in-chat design and explicit yes.

## Project paths

- Specs: `docs/superpowers/specs/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>-design.md`
- Plans: `docs/superpowers/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<feature-name>.md`

## Hospital adaptations

- Default to a feature branch in this worktree. Use `using-git-worktrees` only when the user asks or parallel isolated work needs it (Windows + npm/.NET restore is expensive).
- Do not invent a second test stack, UI kit, or architecture. TDD must extend existing tests.
- Do not put PHI, credentials, or tokens in specs, plans, commits, or logs.
- Brainstorming visual companion telemetry: prefer `SUPERPOWERS_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1` in this environment.
- Subagents must still obey domain ownership and must not touch unrelated modules.
